1. JAVASCRIPT EXECUTOR
----------------------

JavascriptExecutor js = (JavascriptExecutor) driver;

// Scroll down by 1500 pixels
js.executeScript("window.scrollBy(0,1500)");

// Scroll until element is visible
js.executeScript("arguments[0].scrollIntoView()", element);

// Click using JavaScript
js.executeScript("arguments[0].click()", element);

// Set value in textbox
js.executeScript("arguments[0].setAttribute('value','Sameer')", element);

When to Use:
- Element not clickable.
- sendKeys() not working.
- Need to scroll to hidden element.
- DOM manipulation required.

